// gandr has no primitive boolean.
//
// `Bool` is the sum `1 + 1`: `true` is the left injection of unit, `false`
// the right, and the comparison operators return exactly that. Nothing about
// booleans is special-cased in the core -- `if` is sugar over `case`.
//
// The harness renders values *structurally* (the surface pretty-printer is a
// separate, pending piece), so "true" honestly reads as `Inl(())` below.
1 < 2

// The harness checks:
//@ expect: clean
//@ expect-last-value: Inl(())
